.TH "XmeDrawDiamond" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmeDrawDiamond\fP \(em A widget writer function that draws a three-dimensional diamond
.iX "XmeDrawDiamond"
.iX "Xme draw functions" "XmeDrawDiamond"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/DrawP\&.h>
\fBvoid \fBXmeDrawDiamond\fP\fR(
\fBDisplay *\fBdisplay\fR\fR,
\fBDrawable \fBd\fR\fR,
\fBGC \fBtop_gc\fR\fR,
\fBGC \fBbottom_gc\fR\fR,
\fBGC \fBcenter_gc\fR\fR,
\fBPosition \fBx\fR\fR,
\fBPosition \fBy\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBwidth\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBheight\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBshadow_thick\fR\fR,
\fBDimension \fBmargin\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%XmeDrawDiamond\fP draws the diamond-shaped indicator of a
ToggleButton whose \fB\%XmNindicatorType\fP is
\fB\%XmONE_OF_MANY_DIAMOND\fP\&.
The diamond fits in the square of side \fIwidth\fP at \fIx\fP, \fIy\fP;
\fIheight\fP is not used\&.  An even \fIwidth\fP is reduced by one\&.
The upper
edges are drawn with \fItop_gc\fP and the lower edges with
\fIbottom_gc\fP,
each 3 pixels thick\&.  If \fIcenter_gc\fP is not NULL and \fIwidth\fP
is more
than 5, the inside is filled with it, \fImargin\fP pixels inside the
shadow (the margin is ignored when \fIshadow_thick\fP is 0 or 1, for
which the fill covers the shadow)\&.  Nothing is drawn if \fId\fP is
None
or \fIwidth\fP is 0\&.
.IP "\fIdisplay\fP" 10
Specifies the display\&.
.IP "\fId\fP" 10
Specifies the drawable to draw into\&.
.IP "\fItop_gc\fP" 10
Specifies the GC of the upper edges\&.
.IP "\fIbottom_gc\fP" 10
Specifies the GC of the lower edges\&.
.IP "\fIcenter_gc\fP" 10
Specifies the GC of the inside, or NULL\&.
.IP "\fIx\fP" 10
Specifies the x coordinate of the square\&.
.IP "\fIy\fP" 10
Specifies the y coordinate of the square\&.
.IP "\fIwidth\fP" 10
Specifies the side of the square\&.
.IP "\fIheight\fP" 10
Is not used\&.
.IP "\fIshadow_thick\fP" 10
Specifies the shadow thickness of the toggle\&.
.IP "\fImargin\fP" 10
Specifies the space between the shadow and the filled inside\&.
.PP
Motif 1\&.2 called this function \fB\%_XmDrawDiamond\fP\&.  The library
still exports that name for old binaries, and \fB\%<Xm/XmP\&.h>\fP
defines it as a macro for \fB\%XmeDrawDiamond\fP unless
\fB\%NO_XM_1_2_BC\fP is defined; new code should use
\fB\%XmeDrawDiamond\fP\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmeDrawCircle\fP(3), \fB\%XmeDrawIndicator\fP(3) and
\fB\%XmToggleButton\fP(3)\&.
